// ---- Cheats For our Hybrid - New "Main.scm" Code ONLY  (New Button input Cheats) ----
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ---- Dynamic Brightness Cheat  ----
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// * Change Brightness based on weather.

// ---- Adjust Brightness (Menu Option) ----
//Adjust Brightness (Menu Option)
//patch=1,EE,204ADB88,extended,0000011C
//Brightness Max: 					00000180 	|| game default == 00000100
//Brightness Decrease MAX->0 =  	00000167 	|| 14E || 135 || 11C ||103 ||EA ||D1 ||B8 ||9F ||86 ||6D ||54 ||3B ||22 ||09
//Brightness increase 0->MAX =  	00000018 	|| 30 ||48 ||60 ||78 ||90 ||A8 ||C0 ||D8 ||FO ||108 ||120 ||138 ||150 ||168 ||180

//Change weather 							|| This is our "Main.scm" Custom Change Weather Cheat (1-7)
//Input: Press Select + L1 	=	Change weather (1-7)
//patch=1,EE,20555060,extended,00000001 // Actual Weather Number
//patch=1,EE,204E3670,extended,00000001 // Number DISPLAYED

//Dynamic Brightness Cheat == Comparative of weather num with Menu Option "Brightness".
//...	If aaaaaaaa(WeatherNum Address) == vv01(sunny) --> Set aaaaaaaa(brightness Address)  == vvMAX-2 (0000014E) || also set bars displayed in menu.

// * Try to increment & decrement values as they would occur on the menu - in order to retain the correct instructions, this isntruction and value differs depending on direction.
// if you re-order or modify the weather cheats in the scm then the values at these addresses will haev to change accordingly
// See example but in short it (the cheat below) goes: start game default, Increase, Increase, decrease, decrease, decrease, increase back to default.  
// so if you change the 1st sunny to e.g. rainy, that would be a decrease of -3 from default for the brightness in the example below BUT decreasing default by -3 is not the same as what we had previously which was -2 from the already -6, which was taken from the Max
// maybe it is better explained above -  Notice max -1 = 167 when decreasing, but when increase from 1 below max the value is 168
// ^^ so the valeus depend on the direction and therefore the order or your weather cheats.
// * when tested on a clean game, start game, cycle through all 7 options, wait on 7 which is what the gaem would be at the start anyway, enable the cheats below, then switch to weather to 1. Best done in the daytime.
// * once your in the daytime and set back to 1 you can then cyce back to 7 to keep the in-game system normal with the benefit of the brightness patches.
 
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

//Dynamic Brightness Cheat 			|| IF value @ 20555060 == 0x01 --> Write 0x0180 TO 204ADB88
//... 			If weather Sunny set brightness Max -2.
patch=1,EE,E1010001,extended,00555060
patch=1,EE,204ADB88,extended,0000014E
//... 			If weather Extra Sunny set brightness Max.
patch=1,EE,E1010002,extended,00555060
patch=1,EE,204ADB88,extended,00000180
//... 			If weather Cloudy set brightness Max -6.
patch=1,EE,E1010003,extended,00555060
patch=1,EE,204ADB88,extended,000000EA
//... 			If weather Rainy set brightness Max -8.
patch=1,EE,E1010004,extended,00555060
patch=1,EE,204ADB88,extended,000000B8
//... 			If weather Foggy set brightness -4.
patch=1,EE,E1010005,extended,00555060
patch=1,EE,204ADB88,extended,000000D1
//... 			If weather normal 1 (hurricanes off) set brightness Default (max -5).
patch=1,EE,E1010006,extended,00555060
patch=1,EE,204ADB88,extended,00000100
//... 			If weather normal 2  (hurricanes on) set brightness Default (max -5).
patch=1,EE,E1010007,extended,00555060
patch=1,EE,204ADB88,extended,00000100

